# Folded-cascode OTA (one stage), single-ended, NMOS input pair.
# PMOS current sources M3a/M3b (gate pa) feed the folding nodes f1/f2; PMOS cascodes
# M4a/M4b (gate vbp) fold down into an NMOS high-swing cascode mirror (bottom M6a/M6b
# gated by the diode-side cascode drain c1, cascodes M5a/M5b gated by the IREF net).
# VINN drives the output-side half (inverting); VINP the diode side.
# Bias (all from the one IREF): Rb lifts the NMOS cascode gate (= IREF net) above the
# mirror gate n1; M11 copies the reference into the PMOS diode M12 (gate pa = current-
# source gate) and Rp drops the PMOS cascode gate vbp below pa.
NMOS M1a f1 VINP tail
NMOS M1b f2 VINN tail
PMOS M3a f1 pa VDD
PMOS M3b f2 pa VDD
PMOS M4a c1 vbp f1
PMOS M4b VOUT vbp f2
NMOS M5a c1 IREF b1
NMOS M5b VOUT IREF b2
NMOS M6a b1 c1 VSS
NMOS M6b b2 c1 VSS
NMOS M9 tail n1 VSS
NMOS M10 n1 n1 VSS
R Rb IREF n1
NMOS M11 vbp n1 VSS
R Rp pa vbp
PMOS M12 pa pa VDD
